%description:

Tcp.pushSegmentsOnWriteBoundary:long-write -- a write longer than half the largest window has PSH inside it.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "[...] in a write longer than half the largest window (forced_push())".

The classes: off (false, the default), and two facets of on (true; LinuxTcp): write-end, PSH
on the segment that ends a write; long-write, PSH also inside a write longer than half the
largest window. The code: TcpConnection::sendSegment() and the marks of a SEND
(enqueueSendCommandData()). This test separates the facet from "off", with which only
the last segment of the write has PSH.

Host under test: host1, which writes 100000 bytes after its handshake; the largest window of
host2 is 65535 bytes. Observation: level 1, the first data segment with PSH is far from the
end of the write.

%# parameter: Tcp.pushSegmentsOnWriteBoundary
%# class: long-write
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.pushSegmentsOnWriteBoundary
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpPushSegmentsOnWriteBoundaryLongWrite")
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000);
        }))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.1))
        .once(on("host1.app[0]").signal("socketEstablished").within(0.1))
        .act(action().after(0.001).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.sendData(app.socket(), 100000);
        }))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.pshBit == true && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.sequenceNo < {isn} + 1 + 100000 - 2 * 1448")
             .describe("the first data segment with PSH, inside the write")
             .within(1.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpPushSegmentsOnWriteBoundaryLongWrite compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.pushSegmentsOnWriteBoundary = true    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpPushSegmentsOnWriteBoundaryLongWrite: PASS
